X = {}

X["iptv-vs-freeview-and-freesat"] = [
 ("A practical way to choose",["List what you watch. If most of it is on free-to-air channels, you may not need anything else. If you want channels or sport that free-to-air does not carry, IPTV may fill the gap.","Check your own situation too. Flats may not allow dishes, and some homes have poor aerial reception. Internet delivery avoids both problems but needs a good connection."])]

X["iptv-vs-streaming-costs"] = [
 ("A worked example",["Suppose you pay for three on-demand apps and open only one weekly. Cancelling the other two saves their full yearly cost. If you want live channels instead, compare that saving with the total for an IPTV plan. The result is simple arithmetic, not a guess.","Keep a note of the date you cancel. Many services allow you to return later, so cancelling is rarely permanent."])]

X["iptv-box-vs-app"] = [
 ("Simplicity for the household",["If several people use the TV, the simplest setup is the one that starts quickly and has a single remote. A neat box can feel simpler than a TV with several menus, but only if it is well made and updated.","Consider who will fix problems. If that is you, choose the setup you are confident supporting."])]

X["smart-tv-app-vs-streaming-stick"] = [
 ("Age matters",["A TV bought recently may run apps well for years. An older smart TV often falls behind, and a stick can give it a second life for a modest price. Check how old your TV is and whether it still receives updates.","A stick also makes it easier to move your setup when you replace the TV, because it simply goes into the new set."])]

X["iptv-vs-ott-explained"] = [
 ("Why the label matters less than you think",["Companies use the words loosely, so a service described as one or the other tells you little. Focus on what you can verify: which devices it runs on, what the trial covers, how support works and what the refund policy says.","If a seller refuses to explain how their service reaches your screen, treat that as a warning."])]

X["why-quality-varies-by-channel"] = [
 ("How to compare fairly",["Compare channels on the same screen at the same time, and do not judge by a few seconds. Fast moving scenes reveal weaknesses that slow ones hide. Also try the same channel at another time of day, because load can change what you see.","Keep a short list of the channels that look best and use those for the viewing where quality matters most."])]

X["best-settings-for-smooth-playback"] = [
 ("A test routine",["Pick one live channel with plenty of movement. Play it for twenty minutes on your starting settings and note any pauses. Change one setting, for example the buffer size, and repeat. Keep a note, because after three changes it is easy to forget what you did.","If there is no improvement after a couple of changes, the cause is probably the network or the device, not the settings."])]

X["tv-motion-settings-and-sport"] = [
 ("Match the room",["In a bright room, a slightly brighter mode helps. In a dark room, a more natural mode is usually more comfortable. Turn off extreme sharpening, which can create halos around players.","Set your preferences once, write them down and reuse them. Many TVs keep separate settings for each input."])]

X["upscaling-explained"] = [
 ("Realistic expectations",["Upscaling can make a lower resolution picture look acceptable, but it cannot create detail. If you want a genuinely sharp picture, choose channels that carry HD or better. Many people find that after a day of adjusting, they stop noticing.","Do not buy a larger TV hoping that old content will look better. It usually looks softer, not sharper."])]

X["protect-your-router-for-streaming"] = [
 ("A ten minute security session",["Log in to the router, change the admin password, rename the Wi-Fi to something that does not reveal your name, set a long passphrase and check the firmware page. Write down the changes and keep them somewhere safe.","If you are not comfortable making changes, ask your provider for help. A wrong setting can cut off the internet."])]

X["passwords-and-two-factor-for-streaming"] = [
 ("If you think you are compromised",["Change the password at once, sign out of all devices if the service offers it, and change the password on any other account where you used the same one. Check recent activity and payment methods. Contact the service if you see anything you do not recognise.","Keep your recovery email secure too. Anyone who controls it can reset your other passwords."])]

X["public-wifi-and-streaming"] = [
 ("Better alternatives",["If you need to watch while away, consider downloading nothing, using your phone's mobile data for short sessions, or using a travel router you control. For anything involving payment or a password, wait until you are on a trusted connection.","If the network asks you to install software to connect, refuse."])]

X["child-safety-and-streaming"] = [
 ("A family agreement",["Agree simple rules: which rooms devices can be used in, when screens go off and what to do if something upsets them. Children respond better to rules they helped to write.","Review settings after any app or device update, because updates can reset them."])]

X["iptv-for-students-and-shared-houses"] = [
 ("A house agreement",["Write down who pays, which device is the main one and what happens during big events. Check how many streams the plan allows and do not exceed it.","If people come and go during the year, a shorter term may cost slightly more per month but avoids paying for an empty room."])]

X["uk-broadband-outage-what-to-do"] = [
 ("Preparing for the next one",["Save your provider's fault number and outage page on your phone. Keep a spare device with a charged battery. Consider noting your router's make and your account number somewhere you can reach without internet.","If outages are frequent, keep a log. Repeated faults support a request for an engineer visit or a move to another provider."])]

X["uk-consumer-rights-digital-services"] = [
 ("Practical steps if something goes wrong",["Stop, gather evidence and write to the seller clearly, saying what is wrong and what you want. Allow a reasonable time for a reply. If you are not satisfied, use the escalation routes described by official consumer bodies, and your payment provider's process if it applies.","Always keep the tone calm and factual."])]

X["iptv-across-the-four-nations"] = [
 ("Mobile fallback",["If your fixed line is poor, a mobile router or hotspot may work, but data limits and coverage matter. Test at the times you watch. Note that live television can use a lot of data in a short time, so check allowances first."])]

X["uk-sport-calendar-streaming-prep"] = [
 ("A yearly routine",["At the start of each season, update devices, check storage, test the guide and confirm what your plan offers. Add major event dates to your calendar with a reminder to test two days before.","Keeping a short note of what worked, for example the router position and the device, makes next year easier."])]

X["canadian-broadband-for-iptv"] = [
 ("Rural and remote homes",["Some rural homes rely on fixed wireless or satellite, which can have higher delay and weather related drops. Live television needs consistency, so test across several evenings and in different weather.","If your connection is weak, use a lower quality setting and a wired link to the TV. Ask for a trial before paying for a long term."])]

X["iptv-devices-in-canada"] = [
 ("Buying devices in Canada",["When buying a streaming stick or box, check that the listing is for the Canadian market and that you get a warranty. Imported devices may have a different plug or an incompatible app store.","Keep the receipt in case you need to return the device after testing."])]

X["canada-time-zones-and-live-guides"] = [
 ("Travelling across Canada",["If you travel with a tablet or phone, the device may change its time zone automatically. The guide on the app may then shift. This is normal and fixes itself when the time zone is correct.","For events in other time zones, convert before you plan, and set a calendar reminder in your local time."])]

X["iptv-payment-and-currency-canada"] = [
 ("Avoiding surprises",["Check whether your bank adds a foreign transaction fee, because that can change the real cost. Compare two methods before paying if the amount is large. Ask us for the total in pounds and confirm it before you send.","Wise and PayPal both show the exchange rate in advance, which helps you compare."])]

X["can-i-pause-live-tv"] = [
 ("Why pause behaves differently from file playback",["With a film, the whole file exists on a server, so pausing is easy. With a live stream the content is created as it goes, so pausing relies on a buffer. Once the buffer fills, the player may skip forward to live.","If pausing matters to you, test it in your trial and choose an app that supports longer rewind on your device."]),
 ("Tips for short pauses",["Pause for a minute rather than ten. If the stream jumps forward on resume, restart the channel. Keep the device awake with the right power settings."])]

X["how-long-does-iptv-setup-take"] = [
 ("A realistic timeline",["For a prepared household, from receiving details to watching can be a few minutes. For a first time setup on an older device, allow thirty minutes to an hour to cover updates and installs.","If you are setting up for someone else, schedule a calm slot rather than squeezing it in before a match."]),
 ("When it takes longer",["Slow broadband, an old device, typing mistakes and unfamiliar menus add time. None of these means something is wrong."])]

X["why-some-channels-have-no-guide"] = [
 ("Telling a data gap from a fault",["If playback works and only the guide is blank, the video side is fine. The guide is a separate data feed. Try the refresh option, wait a few minutes after first sign in, and check the time zone.","Tell us the channel names and what you see. If the same channels are blank for everyone, we can tell you whether it is a data limitation."])]

X["what-happens-when-subscription-expires"] = [
 ("Planning your renewal",["Decide in advance whether to renew for the same length or try another. Check the {plans} so that you know the total, and compare per-month cost for different lengths. If you are happy with the service, a longer term lowers the monthly cost.","Whatever you decide, do it a few days before the end date so you are not left without access during something you want to watch."])]
